# power-unreachable: per-seed rate and sweep verdict, 300 seeds -- unreachable in the schedule mix the sweep runs, by argument and by measurement. The defect needs a mark opened and then emptied while an earlier gated message waits, which A5's UNTHROTTLED collector produced constantly: 1 detection in 60 seeds. Throttling the collector to one collection in flight -- a 30x runtime win that made a 10,000-seed exit run viable -- took it to 0 in 300 and then 0 in 3000. That is A2's M34 lesson from the other side: a schedule mix is a claim about reachability, and this change traded some. Killed by TestAnEmptyMarkDoesNotReleaseAnEarlierOne, which builds the sequence by hand. RE-MEASURED under current at A6's close with the repaired probe: 0 of 300 per-seed AND sweepfail=0, against a clean baseline of 0 and sweepfail=0 at the same 300 seeds. The opt-out stands. It is NOT M66's or M47's byte-identical unreached, though: 34 census fields drift, so the mutated line runs and the schedule diverges -- what does not occur is the condition the defect needs (DESIGN-A6 section 42). NO OTHER DETECTOR, stated honestly rather than claimed: census identity is NOT available here -- 34 fields drift at 300 seeds, so the mutated line runs and the schedule diverges. What is claimed is narrower: the CONDITION the defect needs does not arise, and the two detectors that could see it if it did -- the per-seed rate and the sweep verdict -- are both silent at 300 against a clean tree that is also silent at 300. The refutation pass adds a third look at 30 seeds and finds the census byte-identical there, which is under-sampling rather than agreement and is recorded as such (DESIGN-A6 section 43.10)
# mutates: a mark that covers nothing releases everything THROUGH it instead of only itself. An empty mark is satisfied because there is nothing to wait for, which is a statement about that mark alone -- it has not earned the monotonicity a durability acknowledgement has. Releasing through it frees messages gated on an earlier mark whose write is still in flight, so a follower advertises a term that is not on its disk (BUG-017)
